+## Install
 
-See `install-to-userdata.sh` and PLAN. Short version: boot the bring-up
-console, then
+From the bring-up console (S-Boot -> uniLoader -> bring-up Linux):
 
 ```sh
 contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh \
-    mkosi.output/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge_*.raw.zst
+    mkosi.output/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge_<ver>.raw
 ```
 
-which streams the image into `/dev/sda31` over USB and verifies the SHA-256,
-then reboot into U-Boot.
+It refuses anything that is not a 4K-sector GPT image, checks on the device
+that sda31 is `PARTNAME=userdata`, streams the image with the console's
+`put`, drops the page cache and reads exactly the image length back to
+compare SHA-256. Every console access takes `build/tab.lock`. It never
+writes anything but `/dev/sda31`.
 
 ## USB debug layer
 
 `duranium-usb-debug` brings up the fixed-MAC NCM interface
-(`fe80::57:aff:fe00:1`), an unauthenticated root console on TCP 23, an sshd on
-22, and a kernel-log stream on 24 — all on the USB link-local address only,
-present in both the initrd and the booted system, enabled by default and
-disable-able (`systemctl disable --now duranium-usb-debug.target`, or ship
-without the package). Security notes in
-`build/wt/pmaports-duranium/main/duranium-usb-debug/README`.
+(`fe80::57:aff:fe00:1`, VID:PID 1d6b:0104, same as the bring-up console), and
+socket-activated services bound to the gadget interface only: a root shell on
+TCP 23 (busybox `telnetd -i -l /bin/sh`), sshd on 22 (inetd mode, own host
+key, booted system only) and the kernel log on 24. The gadget, the shell and
+the kernel log are also in the initrd. On by default; off with
+`systemctl disable --now duranium-usb-debug.target` (booted system) or
+`duranium.usb_debug=0` on the kernel command line (initrd too). Security
+notes: `build/wt/pmaports-duranium/main/duranium-usb-debug/README`.
+
+The address is the bring-up console's, but the protocol is not: TCP 23 is a
+telnet shell, not the bring-up command console, so `scripts/tab`,
+`tab-put` and `tab-get` do not work against Duranium. Use `nc`/`ncat`
+(telnet option bytes may show up as noise) or ssh.
+
+## Safety net (no silent hangs)
+
+| Failure | What resets the device | Where it lands |
+|---|---|---|
+| U-Boot cannot boot the ESP | `fallback` env: watchdog reset | uniLoader -> bring-up Linux (USB console) |
+| Kernel hangs before userspace | U-Boot leaves the cluster 0 watchdog running (~80 s, `wdt_handover=keep`); the kernel pets it only until systemd opens it, at most `watchdog.open_timeout=120` s | Download mode (U-Boot set INFORM3 = 0x12345671 at entry) |
+| Kernel panic / oops | `CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT=3`, `oops=panic` | Download mode (INFORM3 still download) |
+| initrd waits forever (no root disk, no loop device) | `gtactive3wifi-initrd-deadline.service`: 600 s, then `systemctl reboot download` | Download mode |
+| PID 1 hangs | `RuntimeWatchdogSec=30s` | Download mode |
+| Suspend/resume hang | suspend is disabled (sleep.conf.d, logind.conf.d) | - |
+
+Not a reset: a hang of the booted system while PID 1 keeps running (e.g.
+phosh frozen). That case is reached over the USB debug layer instead.
+
